You are given a task to integrate a component from the **kinetik** motion library into this codebase.

# Chart — Funnel (`chart-funnel`)

Conversion funnel drawn as one continuous, smoothly tapering SVG shape: stages pour in from the top on view, drop-off between stages appears as a pill, and hovering a stage highlights its band and shows its share of the top.

## What it should do
For each stage build a path from its half-width to the next stage's with cubic curves on both sides; animate scaleY from the band's top with a stagger; compute drop-off between consecutive stages.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **svg**.
- Install dependencies: `npm i motion`
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/chart-funnel.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** SVG has an aria-label listing all stages; stage rows are focusable buttons. Reduced motion shows the final chart.
- **Performance:** Five paths and a short list; animations run once.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

